** Uniaxial tension of the 10 x 20 x 30 mm box, meshed by GridForge's
** mesher (gf_mesh, Netgen) with quadratic tetrahedra and written by its
** deck writer: mesh.inp, from
**   gf-study mesh tests/fixtures/step/box.step --size 5 --order 2 --inp
** This deck around it is written by hand.
**
** Symmetry planes hold x = 0 (Face1) in x, y = 0 (Face3) in y and z = 0
** (Face5) in z; x = 10 (Face2) is pulled 0.01 mm in x. Steel, E = 210000
** MPa, nu = 0.3. Known by hand, at every node:
**   ux = 0.001 x;  uy = -0.0003 y;  uz = -0.0003 z
**   stress xx = 210 MPa, every other component 0
**   the reaction on Face2: 210 MPa * 20 mm * 30 mm = 126000 N in x
*INCLUDE, INPUT=mesh.inp
*MATERIAL, NAME=STEEL
*ELASTIC
210000, 0.3
*SOLID SECTION, ELSET=Solid1, MATERIAL=STEEL
*BOUNDARY
Face1, 1, 1, 0
Face3, 2, 2, 0
Face5, 3, 3, 0
*STEP
*STATIC
*BOUNDARY
Face2, 1, 1, 0.01
*NODE FILE
U, RF
*EL FILE
S, E
*NODE PRINT, NSET=Face2, TOTALS=ONLY
RF
*END STEP
